WEBVTT

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.030
<i>Maybe I can handle it 
just once, right now.</i>

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.400
<i>I'm sorry, Ryuuka.</i>

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.320
<i>Double.</i>

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.310
<i>Two turns in the future!</i>

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.620
<i>Shindouji.</i>

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.410
Pon!

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.050
Pon!

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:17.680
<i>This is what I have to do since 
I'm seated after Miyanaga Teru.</i>

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.310
<i>Shindouji is going out on a limb...</i>

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:29.770
<i>Pon again!</i>

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.540
<i>One more time.</i>

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.300
I did it.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:16.860
Pon!

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.120
<i>"I did it" isn't quite right... 
It's more like...</i>

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.760
<i>Shindouji enabled me to.</i>

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.220
<i>This is it.</i>

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.850
Tsumo. 2,300. 4,200.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.900
Senriyama's Onjouji has put a stop 
to the champion's dealer's streak!

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.150
She won!

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.000
Senpai!

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:54.860
She did it!

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.110
Toki.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.040
Don't tell me you...

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.280
<i>I'm sorry, Shindouji.</i>

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.210
<i>I couldn't tell what that tile was...</i>

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.490
<i>It's fine.</i>

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.910
<i>Marvelous.</i>

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.060
<i>If she had called a riichi, 
it would have been an ippatsu tsumo.</i>

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.210
<i>She ignored her signature 
move just to win.</i>

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.720
We're in the South round now!

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.920
We're finally in the second 
half's South round!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.030
South Hand 1

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.030
Dealer:  Hanada Kirame

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.840
Which means we've only got four 
more hands left in this match!

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.870
Turn 5

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:15.190
<b>Round 11:
Determination</b>

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.900
<i>I never thought drawing 
a tile could be so hard.</i>

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.790
<i>I'm losing strength.</i>

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.920
<i>One more time.</i>

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.310
<i>I couldn't stop it.</i>

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:29.970
Ron!

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.930
Y-Yes!

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:32.970
1,300.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.310
<i>Three more hands to go.</i>

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:41.820
<i>This could actually be really bad.</i>

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:46.860
You think Hanada's going 
to be okay, president?

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.000
Even with a biased outlook, 
I don't think so...

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.420
I wonder why Hanada was put

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.240
as the first player at Nationals.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.600
The other players are also 
different from last year.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.520
Huh, president?

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.560
The first player is a sacrifice.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.180
What?

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:21.440
For years now, our school never 
did well at Nationals.

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:25.440
Our ace player was always defeated 
by the other schools' aces.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.150
There are schools, like Himematsu, 
where the ace

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.220
traditionally is the third player,

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.660
and schools where the ace plays last,

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.990
but we never cared about those traditions,

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:40.200
and always had the ace play first.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.750
We've always lost there.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.500
Last year, I failed there.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.570
That's why we're changing our strategy.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.050
It was too frustrating.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.640
That's why this year,

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.560
our teacher said that we're 
putting our strongest players

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.750
in reverse order and
 sacrificing the first player...

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:04.520
Then why isn't Tomokiyo, 
who ranks 5th, on our team?

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.550
Do you remember that practice match 
we had a while back with the pros?

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.950
Uh, yes.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.320
There was only one person who managed

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.790
to never go bust after two 
days of playing pros.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.250
Hanada was the only one.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:25.000
If you ask her, she'll tell you that 
she's never lost all her points.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.500
She will not go bust.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.300
So that's why

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.410
she was put in first as the sacrifice.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.220
Hanada would be so depressed 
if she heard that.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.720
She was so happy when 
she was made a regular.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:40.040
That's why we have to fight

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.980
with the power of the remaining four.

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:47.690
Whoops, I overheard.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.130
That's a shock.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.990
Just kidding!

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:59.940
<i>I'm glad. I have an ability 
that somebody needs.</i>

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.750
<i>It's not an ability that'll make me the ace...</i>

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.360
<i>But it's needed.</i>

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.230
<i>There's nothing more 
marvelous than that.</i>

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:12.300
<i>I'll be the sacrificial pawn!</i>

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:12.670
South Hand 2

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.300
<i>Should I focus on</i>

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.890
<i>keeping the points lost to
 an absolute minimum,</i>

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.740
<i>or should I go out on a limb</i>

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:24.400
<i>within the limits of not going bust?</i>

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.120
<i>I don't know!
 Oh, this is fun!</i>

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.800
<i>Since my hand looks like 
this after five turns,</i>

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:31.650
<i>I might as well go on the attack!</i>

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:34.890
Ron.

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:36.850
So fast! Marvelous!

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:36.340
<b>Marvelous</b>

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:38.280
2,600.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:39.910
Yes.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.250
South Hand 3

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.750
<i>There are only two hands left.</i>

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:48.750
<i>What am I supposed to do with this?</i>

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:50.650
<i>We're one hand before the last.</i>

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:53.260
<i>Is there nothing I can do?</i>

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:01.790
Tsumo.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:04.050
1,300. 2,600.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.360
<i>This time, I couldn't 
even see one turn ahead.</i>

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:14.370
<i>Maybe... I can't do it anymore.</i>

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.570
Now we're in the very last hand!

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.990
It's the player who has 
close to 200,000 points,

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.120
the champion's, turn to be dealer!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.150
<b>Senriyama Girls'</b>

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.150
This can't go on...

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.460
I didn't expect the gap 
to get that big.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:54.320
No, I'm talking about Toki!

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.020
If this keeps going, her body will...

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:56.950
<i>Ron.</i>

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.950
7,700.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.470
<i>Onjouji-san.</i>

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.690
<i>Senriyama's ace?</i>

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:16.720
Toki just...

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.590
Toki played into her hand?

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.900
Senriyama's Onjouji just played into

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:23.660
another player's hand without 
having declared riichi!

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.350
In her official games, this 
has never happened before!

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.440
A real first time!

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.810
Did you have to emphasize it like that?

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:36.640
The final dealer decides 
to continue playing!

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.530
Considering the team tournament rules

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:43.740
and having this huge lead in the first 
players' match, that makes sense...

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:52.330
<i>Could it be possible that 
Toki can't see it anymore?</i>

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.690
We're...

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.110
...here!

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:26.870
Let's hurry up and go in.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.190
Huh? What's wrong, Saki-chan?

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.130
Uh, I...

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:42.430
Saki-san?

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.140
Let's hurry up and go in!

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:47.180
Uh, I'm... just...

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.140
Why don't you two go ahead?

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.900
I'll come soon, I promise.

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.800
If you need a bathroom, 
they have them inside.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:58.230
All right.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.020
Yuuki, let's go.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:00.880
All right!

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.740
See you later, Saki-chan!

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:20.380
<i>It looks like the stage belongs 
completely to the champion.</i>

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.800
<i>How long will her dealer's 
streak last this time?</i>

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.680
Do you think those girls made it by now?

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:31.060
I feel like they messed up 
big time with the trains...

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:32.750
Timing-wise it's not quite clear

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:35.810
if they'll make it before the 
first players' match is over.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:40.940
But it's impossible to tell when 
this match will even be over.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:46.820
Do you think the champion 
will keep winning like this?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.870
Then it would be faster 
if someone just went bust.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.310
Yeah.

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:54.250
<i>But if we keep winning,</i>

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.050
<i>we'll have to play against her eventually.</i>

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.870
<i>What can we do to stop her?</i>

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:02.630
<i>Shiraitodai has just broken 
the 200,000 point mark!</i>

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.070
But of course, the champion rejects

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:09.230
ending the match and 
continues play as dealer!

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:14.160
She is really pulverizing the 
other players singlehandedly!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.210
<i>Ryuuka,</i>

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:21.020
<i>I might... be at my end...</i>

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.190
"Toki shift"?

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:25.990
Yeah!

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:27.760
What is that?

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.620
It means we're shifting 
our schedules around

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.410
to be able to support you, our ace.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.140
That was the condition for

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.930
your doctor to allow you 
to go to the mahjong camp.

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:39.540
Of course, we'll start while 
we're still in school.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.580
Oh, then I won't have to

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:44.850
commute from the hospital to the school.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:46.550
That's the idea.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:50.480
I've already researched 
your food for the camp.

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:53.720
The nutritionist from the 
hospital gave us some pointers.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:57.810
I'm a pretty good cook,
 so I'll help with the food.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:00.560
And you can count on me 
to do any physical work.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:07.280
That makes me happy, but I feel bad...

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:09.300
If someone has to do all this,

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:12.080
wouldn't it be better 
if someone else did it?

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.190
Coach was saying

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:15.670
that we should have the 
bench players do it, too.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.710
I, too, think that would be the most

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:19.920
efficient and rational solution.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.420
Still, we want to do it.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:25.500
FunaQ...

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:27.720
Something good might come

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.180
from just spending time together, as well.

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:32.190
That's completely unscientific.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:36.730
You're the one who just 
said something illogical.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.440
<i>My teammates...</i>

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.840
Illogical is not the same as unscientific.

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.920
What's the difference?

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.010
<i>are doing this for me.</i>

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:44.700
Everyone...

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.830
Thanks.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.910
The mosquitoes will eat you alive 
if you hang around out here.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:41.420
It seems like a shame to sleep now.

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:45.020
Wouldn't it be more of a shame to 
miss your bath in the morning?

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.050
We can do both if we stay up all night,

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.750
but then tomorrow would be rough.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.050
That's why you're elegantly 
enjoying the night?

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.430
I was looking at the lights.

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:57.640
What lights?

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:02.000
Look! On the other side of the river, 
you can see all these lights.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:05.320
Behind each one of them is a family.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.610
Like, each one is someone's life...

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.770
They might all be street and traffic lights.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.370
Can't you let me pretend?

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:26.420
Sera was saying...

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.990
That last year, on the plane back

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:31.670
after losing the championship...

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:36.010
she saw the sea of lights out the window.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.800
She said that there was probably

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.260
at least one person down 
there who rooted for her.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.570
When she thought of it 
that way, she felt so sad

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:48.010
and upset with herself for letting 
them down, she couldn't take it.

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:51.440
That's not like her.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:53.950
Yeah...

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:57.570
Maybe that's just what 
Nationals do to you.

00:16:58.090 --> 00:16:59.160
What are you talking about?

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:01.410
That's a cold stare!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.790
Still, if Sera said so, 
I guess I'll take a look

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:10.030
out the airplane's 
window on the way back.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.130
<i>It's just coming to my turn.</i>

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:44.290
<i>I wasn't out for a whole turn, then.</i>

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:50.460
<i>I guess that was like a flash nap...</i>

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:08.900
<i>I'm somehow only one tile from tenpai.</i>

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:13.940
<i>She's going to tsumo!</i>

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:32.920
Tsumo.

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.420
4,100 from everyone.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.960
<i>The champion strikes again!</i>

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:43.770
<i>She is now 130,000 points ahead 
of the second place player!</i>

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:48.490
<i>Nobody, nobody can put 
a stop to this monster!</i>

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:49.410
Kuro.

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:50.350
Kuro-chan.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:52.900
<i>Hang in there, Kuro-san!</i>

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:56.490
Last hand, bonus 2!

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:02.240
She will not let go of her 
prey until it's dead!

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:04.220
She will keep going!

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:08.040
Until she squeezes the 
breath out of someone!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.750
That's the expression on her face!

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:12.670
You weren't even looking at the 
monitor when you said that!

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.010
South Hand 4

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.010
Bonus 2

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.640
<i>I can see a little bit again.</i>

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:34.860
<i>Her last win was 12,300,</i>

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:40.250
<i>which means her next win 
would be at least 18,600.</i>

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:45.950
<i>I have to do it.</i>

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.550
<i>I can't just let Miyanaga 
Teru keep winning.</i>

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.730
<i>If this goes on, someone will go bust</i>

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.460
<i>and the whole match will be over.</i>

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:58.020
<i>The probability of me ending 
up in second place,</i>

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:57.460
<b>Marvelous</b>

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:01.220
<i>and the probability of the others rallying 
so we end in second or better...</i>

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:01.240
<b>Marvelous</b>

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:05.470
<i>I'm not smart enough to calculate 
and compare those odds,</i>

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:09.260
<i>but there's one thing I do understand.</i>

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:12.440
<i>The outcome that I'd be happiest with!</i>

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:14.810
<i>I'm not going to let her 
make anyone go bust!</i>

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:19.700
<i>I haven't won even once today!</i>

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:23.990
<i>I will have been completely useless!</i>

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:26.180
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:30.970
<i>You're really beating 
yourself up over there,</i>

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:33.370
<i>but you helped us out so much today.</i>

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.950
<i>Because Achiga kept hoarding the dora,</i>

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:39.170
<i>the other hands were easier to read</i>

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:42.120
<i>and the champion couldn't 
raise her score with dora.</i>

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:47.140
<i>She'll have to start overreaching 
herself to get that higher score.</i>

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:49.600
<i>That's what I hope, anyway.</i>

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.660
<i>I don't remember the 
tiles being this heavy.</i>

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:07.830
<i>It's hard to be alive.</i>

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:12.530
You've found the truth 
at quite a young age.

00:21:12.530 --> 00:21:14.240
But we want to do it.

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:15.400
Something good might come

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:17.580
from just spending time together, as well.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.510
That's not like her.

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:21.510
But maybe that's what the 
Nationals do to you.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.630
<i>You're right, Ryuuka.</i>

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:27.890
<i>Now is when I need</i>

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.020
<i>the one turn ahead sight 
that you all gave me.</i>

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:35.970
<i>I'm sorry, everyone,</i>

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.230
<i>but I'm going to risk it one more time.</i>

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:42.370
Don't! Don't!

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:44.100
Stop, Toki!

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:55.620
<i>Triple...</i>

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:59.000
<i>three turns ahead!</i>

00:23:22.860 --> 00:23:25.070
Day 7 - Block A
 Semifinals

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:32.040
Damn... we can't go inside!

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:34.220
I guess that's the semifinals for you.

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.050
Only morning and it's already like this.

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:37.390
Since it's come to this,

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:39.270
it looks like we'll have to use the power

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:40.750
of your boobs to get us in!

00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:42.190
What are you talking about?

00:23:42.550 --> 00:23:43.820
I understand.

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:45.930
Just send it as is.

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:50.430
Getting mad will just make 
your boobs get bigger.

00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:51.860
No, they won't!

00:23:52.630 --> 00:23:54.620
They're getting bigger.

00:23:53.220 --> 00:23:54.620
<i>Those girls...</i>

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:19.930
<b>Promise</b>

